    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0459" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg451"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9963: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-07T17:00:00+08:00">September 7, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 7—12:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Embassy was informed yesterday by the Minister of Foreign Affairs that “The
                    Chinese Government has, in view of the present tense situation, closed to
                    navigation the mouth of the Min Kiang, in <pb facs="0460" n="452" xml:id="pg452"
                    /> Fukien Province, and that all shipping through that place has been suspended
                    as from September 4”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
